 If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFingering":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFingering"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFingering","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLFingering","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFingering","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfingering","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Fingering is typically indicated 1,2,3,4,5. Multiple fingerings may be given, typically to substitute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingerings in the middle of a note. The substitution and alternate values are “no” if the attribute is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"present. For guitar and other fretted instruments, the fingering element represents the fretting finger; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pluck element represents the plucking finger.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFingering/color":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfingering\/color","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFingering\/color","kind":"symbol","title":"color","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"t